00:10:24.938 --> 00:10:27.377
of mind, body and spirit?

00:10:27.377 --> 00:10:29.830
You know, you're a big
inspiration to me, Gary,

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:32.187
I follow you and a lot of your posts

00:10:32.187 --> 00:10:34.496
throughout the social media platforms

00:10:34.496 --> 00:10:37.107
and yeah, that's the question

00:10:37.107 --> 00:10:38.498
I have for you--
- I appreciate it, brother,

00:10:38.498 --> 00:10:39.399
I appreciate it.

00:10:39.399 --> 00:10:43.048
So, mind, body and spirit,
and health, all that.

00:10:43.048 --> 00:10:45.844
So, until six years ago,
my body, definitely not.

00:10:45.844 --> 00:10:47.141
And I really got serious about health

00:10:47.141 --> 00:10:48.607
and fitness on that level.

00:10:48.607 --> 00:10:51.488
On the mind and happiness side, for sure.

00:10:51.488 --> 00:10:54.790
This thing has been the
driving force for me forever.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.035
For me, definition of happiness

00:10:57.035 --> 00:11:00.062
is the ability to do what
you want to do every day.

00:11:00.062 --> 00:11:02.180
Which is just a remarkable gift,

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.865
which is why I want so
many more people to go

00:11:04.865 --> 00:11:06.595
into their passion and not worry

00:11:06.595 --> 00:11:08.324
about making a million dollars,

00:11:08.324 --> 00:11:10.997
but worry about making a million smiles

00:11:10.997 --> 00:11:13.238
in their lifetime, right?

00:11:13.238 --> 00:11:15.602
To me, the definition of happiness

00:11:15.602 --> 00:11:17.852
for me is leaving a legacy.

00:11:21.301 --> 00:11:22.698
There's so many contemporaries

00:11:22.698 --> 00:11:23.981
I have in entrepreneur land,

00:11:23.981 --> 00:11:27.199
who have no interest in
producing any content, Zane,

00:11:27.199 --> 00:11:29.456
in doing any mentoring,

00:11:29.456 --> 00:11:31.163
and it's so foreign to me.

00:11:31.163 --> 00:11:35.142
They'd rather build empires
continuously for themselves,

00:11:35.142 --> 00:11:36.737
and the people associated with them,

00:11:36.737 --> 00:11:40.375
which I respect, 'cause I
absolutely have that gear in me.

00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:42.904
But for me, I'd be so unhappy if I didn't

00:11:42.904 --> 00:11:44.468
do "Tea With GaryVee" for free,

00:11:44.468 --> 00:11:46.049
if I didn't put out all the content,

00:11:46.049 --> 00:11:48.420
if I didn't try to leave a legacy,

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.414
If I didn't live a world
where I was getting emails

00:11:50.414 --> 00:11:53.125
from kids that were
inspired and started stuff.

00:11:53.125 --> 00:11:57.013
I have so much happiness
inside of me that I feel,

00:11:57.013 --> 00:11:58.830
this is to shoot it
straight with you Zane,

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:02.208
a balance between
gratitude and even guilt.

00:12:02.208 --> 00:12:04.465
You know, I understand that
the chemicals I was given

00:12:04.465 --> 00:12:05.298
were right,

00:12:05.298 --> 00:12:07.261
I understand the circumstances
of being an immigrant

00:12:07.261 --> 00:12:10.722
to work right, which made me hungry.

00:12:10.722 --> 00:12:12.186
You don't get to pick your parents,

00:12:12.186 --> 00:12:13.456
I won that game.

00:12:13.456 --> 00:12:15.716
So, you know, it's really hard for me

00:12:15.716 --> 00:12:17.540
to not have a level of like,

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.888
"Wow, I have to give back."

00:12:19.888 --> 00:12:22.730
Honestly, giving back
financially once you make it

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.327
is the easy part, if you can afford it,

00:12:24.327 --> 00:12:25.614
writing a check.

00:12:25.614 --> 00:12:27.761
I'm proud of the things I've
been doing during this time,

00:12:27.761 --> 00:12:28.756
I keep that stuff quiet.

00:12:28.756 --> 00:12:32.651
But punchline is buying
10s of thousands of masks

00:12:32.651 --> 00:12:33.582
and donating them

00:12:33.582 --> 00:12:36.425
comes a little bit easier
when you can afford it.

00:12:36.425 --> 00:12:37.459
It's putting the time in.

00:12:37.459 --> 00:12:39.257
Right now, I have a lot of fires.

00:12:39.257 --> 00:12:40.830
I have a very intense day today.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:41.836
I have big responsibilities

00:12:41.836 --> 00:12:44.291
in maintaining people's jobs
and growing the company,

00:12:44.291 --> 00:12:47.662
but I feel compelled to give
these two hours every morning

00:12:47.662 --> 00:12:49.402
because as stressed as I am,

00:12:49.402 --> 00:12:51.399
and as much as the gray
hairs are coming in

00:12:51.399 --> 00:12:53.503
doing this kind of time,

00:12:53.503 --> 00:12:55.304
I know that in these two hours,

00:12:55.304 --> 00:12:56.633
a lot of good is being done.

00:12:56.633 --> 00:13:00.199
There's a lot of people that
need my energy right now.

00:13:00.199 --> 00:13:01.737
I can feel it.

00:13:01.737 --> 00:13:03.990
And so I fucking have to do it.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.107
- Man, that's right, you guys, your energy

00:13:06.107 --> 00:13:07.530
definitely picks me up,

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.367
and you know that's a question

00:13:09.367 --> 00:13:12.175
that actually hits home with me as well,

00:13:12.175 --> 00:13:13.936
you know, as a professional athlete,

00:13:13.936 --> 00:13:15.702
you even mentioned as well, you know,

00:13:15.702 --> 00:13:19.611
that balance between guilt
and you said the balance--

00:13:19.611 --> 00:13:21.617
- Gratitude.
- Guilt and gratitude.

00:13:21.617 --> 00:13:25.066
And you know, my grandmother
always inspired me

00:13:25.066 --> 00:13:28.464
to live life with the
attitude of gratitude and--

00:13:28.464 --> 00:13:29.464
- Love that.

00:13:30.923 --> 00:13:32.498
I think gratitude,

00:13:32.498 --> 00:13:36.365
if gratitude and compassion and empathy

00:13:36.365 --> 00:13:39.496
can become bigger, cooler words,

00:13:39.496 --> 00:13:41.498
I think we can really win this game.

00:13:41.498 --> 00:13:43.983
We just need a lot more
kindness in our society.

00:13:43.983 --> 00:13:48.156
There's so much judgment and
there's so much triggering

00:13:48.156 --> 00:13:50.980
to blame, there's so much anxiety.

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:53.308
And a lot of that comes
from actual entitlement.

00:13:53.308 --> 00:13:55.515
If we were grateful for what we had,

00:13:55.515 --> 00:13:58.598
versus envious of what we don't have,

00:14:00.434 --> 00:14:02.106
and the things that people envy

00:14:02.106 --> 00:14:05.117
are such fucking materialistic horseshit.

00:14:05.117 --> 00:14:07.825
I wish people knew more multimillionaires

00:14:07.825 --> 00:14:10.688
and realized how much
unhappiness is at that level.

00:14:10.688 --> 00:14:13.027
If they really knew it,
if they really lived it,

00:14:13.027 --> 00:14:14.754
if they really lived that anxiety

00:14:14.754 --> 00:14:17.690
and insecurity of most, not all of course,

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.107
they would not aspire for it.

00:14:21.182 --> 00:14:22.713
- Yeah, totally.

00:14:22.713 --> 00:14:24.377
Well, I really appreciate that--

00:14:24.377 --> 00:14:25.210
- Zane, I appreciate you, man.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.610
- Sharing your time with us.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.098
- I wish you nothing
but the best, brother.

00:14:29.098 --> 00:14:32.285
Take care my friend, stay well.

00:14:32.285 --> 00:14:33.991
Nick, thanks for being in the comments.

00:14:33.991 --> 00:14:36.537
Geno Productions, big shout out to you.

00:14:36.537 --> 00:14:39.560
I see you in the YouTube comments.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:43.657
Shark Carter. Great to
see you, Shalone Carson.

00:14:43.657 --> 00:14:46.747
Polina Why, thank you so much
for being on YouTube with us.

00:14:46.747 --> 00:14:49.446
Crafty Belfast, what's good? Janelle.

