I think about business.

00:16:10.837 --> 00:16:12.190
And my business is booming,

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:14.069
like people are reading more books now.

00:16:14.069 --> 00:16:16.320
And I picked up two new clients

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:17.885
since this whole pandemic has started.

00:16:17.885 --> 00:16:19.483
So, I'm in a really good spot.

00:16:19.483 --> 00:16:22.382
And I don't know, I don't
know what you think.

00:16:22.382 --> 00:16:23.423
I listen to your stuff all the time,

00:16:23.423 --> 00:16:26.763
and I was like, "What would
Gary say in this situation?"

00:16:26.763 --> 00:16:29.185
about kind of balancing those two.

00:16:29.185 --> 00:16:31.327
- I would do them both.

00:16:31.327 --> 00:16:33.746
And I would be okay
with if I'm in a moment

00:16:33.746 --> 00:16:38.603
in my business that I go all
in for 87% on the business

00:16:38.603 --> 00:16:40.451
and 13 on writing on the side.

00:16:40.451 --> 00:16:42.733
Or even, by the way, 100.

00:16:42.733 --> 00:16:45.711
You know, my great love in
business is Wine Library.

00:16:45.711 --> 00:16:48.823
It was my first love, it
was my family business.

00:16:48.823 --> 00:16:50.020
I went super hard.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:52.612
And then I left and started VaynerMedia.

00:16:52.612 --> 00:16:54.303
And during that time,

00:16:54.303 --> 00:16:57.019
especially the years
three, four, five, six

00:16:57.019 --> 00:16:58.714
and seven of VaynerMedia,

00:16:58.714 --> 00:17:00.907
I really went all in on VaynerMedia.

00:17:00.907 --> 00:17:01.740
Because years one and two,

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:03.257
I still had too many responsibilities,

00:17:03.257 --> 00:17:04.939
I had to make sure Brandon and my dad

00:17:04.939 --> 00:17:06.716
were good on Wine Library without me,

00:17:06.716 --> 00:17:07.777
'cause I was really the leader there.

00:17:07.777 --> 00:17:11.027
And then, a year ago, I just missed it.

00:17:12.407 --> 00:17:15.249
I missed wine commerce
and I invented Wine Text,

00:17:15.249 --> 00:17:17.134
you know, for my dad.

00:17:17.134 --> 00:17:20.125
And so you might be able
to write in three years.

00:17:20.125 --> 00:17:22.423
I think people make the mistake

00:17:22.423 --> 00:17:24.430
and they think balance is a daily thing.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:27.016
Balance is a life thing.

00:17:27.016 --> 00:17:29.382
It's your whole life.

00:17:29.382 --> 00:17:31.580
You're such a young woman.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:33.813
Like, you might be able to
build your business up right now

00:17:33.813 --> 00:17:35.614
to so much stability and save money

00:17:35.614 --> 00:17:37.602
that you might be able to, in 11 years,

00:17:37.602 --> 00:17:41.728
take two years off and
write your fucking novel.

00:17:41.728 --> 00:17:44.563
- I guess--
- People, go ahead.

00:17:44.563 --> 00:17:45.427
- I don't know.

00:17:45.427 --> 00:17:47.416
I fear that if I let it go for too long,

00:17:47.416 --> 00:17:49.249
it'll just be it and--

00:17:50.509 --> 00:17:52.580
- Passions don't die.

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:54.016
Passions are your best friend.

00:17:54.016 --> 00:17:55.306
They're sitting there, waiting for you,

00:17:55.306 --> 00:17:57.223
whenever you come back.

00:17:59.697 --> 00:18:00.828
They are, they're your best friends.

00:18:00.828 --> 00:18:02.106
They're always there.

00:18:02.106 --> 00:18:04.166
Sports cards have been
there, wine have been there.

00:18:04.166 --> 00:18:04.999
You know?

00:18:04.999 --> 00:18:07.223
Seven years ago, I went all GaryVee, 100%.

00:18:07.223 --> 00:18:10.550
Built a humongous company,
have nothing but opportunity,

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.868
could go on and do all sorts of things.

00:18:12.868 --> 00:18:14.535
And here I am at 44,

00:18:15.867 --> 00:18:17.963
and two of the biggest things I talk about

00:18:17.963 --> 00:18:19.520
are wine and sports cards,

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:22.671
my passions from when I was 15.

00:18:22.671 --> 00:18:24.599
Two things that were not
coming out of my mouth

00:18:24.599 --> 00:18:27.396
at all three years ago and
four years ago for the year.

00:18:27.396 --> 00:18:29.555
I have a funny feeling, if
you look at all my content

00:18:29.555 --> 00:18:30.731
three and four years ago,

00:18:30.731 --> 00:18:33.872
I'm not sure if there's
a single mention of wine

00:18:33.872 --> 00:18:36.624
or baseball cards, or sports cards.

00:18:36.624 --> 00:18:38.202
Passions are always there.

00:18:38.202 --> 00:18:39.740
They're just sitting over
there, your best friend,

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:41.142
just waiting for you to sit by the bench,

00:18:41.142 --> 00:18:44.015
some fucking "Forrest Gump" shit.

00:18:44.015 --> 00:18:44.945
Know what I'm saying?

00:18:44.945 --> 00:18:47.051
- I understand (laughs).

00:18:47.051 --> 00:18:50.076
- Balancing everybody
debates on a daily basis.

00:18:50.076 --> 00:18:51.792
It's their number one mistake.

00:18:51.792 --> 00:18:53.612
It's not a daily thing.
It's not a weekly thing.

00:18:53.612 --> 00:18:54.585
It's not a monthly thing.

00:18:54.585 --> 00:18:55.686
It's not even a yearly thing.

00:18:55.686 --> 00:18:57.251
It is a full-life thing.

00:18:57.251 --> 00:18:58.998
Your business is rocking right now.

00:18:58.998 --> 00:19:02.046
It's okay to go 100% in for 36 months.

00:19:02.046 --> 00:19:04.693
I promise you, pen and paper, laptop,

00:19:04.693 --> 00:19:06.362
and fucking Word documents are sitting

00:19:06.362 --> 00:19:08.458
right there waiting for you, open arms,

00:19:08.458 --> 00:19:10.602
with a big hug and kiss and ready to go.

00:19:10.602 --> 00:19:12.262
And by the way, you'll be a
different woman at that point.

00:19:12.262 --> 00:19:15.754
And you might be able to be in a situation

00:19:15.754 --> 00:19:18.921
where you might be even more creative.

00:19:21.142 --> 00:19:24.529
- Yeah, can I ask you a
business question then?

00:19:24.529 --> 00:19:25.362
- You can.

00:19:26.479 --> 00:19:28.823
- I interviewed someone last week

00:19:28.823 --> 00:19:31.365
to be my second full-time person.

00:19:31.365 --> 00:19:34.195
And I had kind of started
recruiting months ago,

00:19:34.195 --> 00:19:35.750
before all this happened.

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.266
And I found a person that
I think would do well

00:19:37.266 --> 00:19:38.649
but I don't know now

00:19:38.649 --> 00:19:41.897
if it's the time to take
on a full-time staff.

00:19:41.897 --> 00:19:44.338
Like what I said, things
are moving up for me,

00:19:44.338 --> 00:19:45.171
but I don't know if--

00:19:45.171 --> 00:19:47.594
- I think as long as you
over-communicate with her,

00:19:47.594 --> 00:19:49.043
like, "Hey, things are moving up for me,

00:19:49.043 --> 00:19:52.030
"but it's uncertain,
anything could happen.

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:53.474
"I don't want to screw you.

00:19:53.474 --> 00:19:55.131
"This is not the most stable situation,

00:19:55.131 --> 00:19:56.987
"plus I'm a small company."

00:19:56.987 --> 00:20:00.404
And give her the right to choose, or him.

00:20:01.257 --> 00:20:04.170
- Where do you get your
clarity from? (laughs)

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:05.346
- You know what's funny,

00:20:05.346 --> 00:20:07.898
I actually think, besides natural DNA,

00:20:07.898 --> 00:20:09.983
and I always think I was born with wisdom,

00:20:09.983 --> 00:20:11.233
I do think I'm an old soul,

00:20:11.233 --> 00:20:13.640
I was very attracted to older
people when I was little,

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:15.410
I would always hang out with
like grandmas and grandpas

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:18.063
on the playground in
New York, in New Jersey.

00:20:18.063 --> 00:20:20.662
Besides that, I actually
think it's a little bit

00:20:20.662 --> 00:20:22.188
